[00:07.89] The scattered pages of a book by the sea
[00:14.82] Held by the sand, washed by the waves
[00:19.34] A shadow forms cast by a cloud
[00:25.48] Skimming by as eyes of the past, but the rising tide
[00:33.05] Absorbs them effortlessly claiming
[00:37.93] They told of one who tired of all singing
[00:42.63] "Praise him, praise him"
[00:45.18] "We heed not flatterers," he cried
[00:50.05] "By our command, waters retreat
[00:56.25] Show my power, halt at my feet"
[01:02.17] But the cause was lost
[01:04.12] Now cold winds blow
[01:08.51] For from the north overcast ranks advance
[01:14.51] Fear of the storm accusing with rage and scorn
[01:20.94] The waves surround the sinking throne
[01:25.06] Singing "Crown him, crown him"
[01:28.92] "Those who love our majesty show themselves"
[01:38.22] All bent their knees
[01:41.63] But he forced a smile even though
[01:45.66] 
[03:14.41] His hopes lay dashed where offerings fell (where they fell)
[03:26.26] 
[04:58.27] "Nothing can my peace destroy as long as none smile"
[05:06.22] More opened ears and opened eyes
[05:11.33] And soon they dared to laugh
[05:17.58] 
[05:29.93] See a little man with his face turning red
[05:31.98] Though his story's often told you can tell he's dead
[05:34.51] 